  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What it works out",
      "items": [
        "element(i, j) is at position (i * n) + j",
        "(A + B)(i,j) = A(i,j) + B(i,j)",
        "(A * B)(i,j) = sum over k of A(i,k) * B(k,j)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "What follows from the layout",
      "items": [
        "A row is a run of n values side by side, thus walking one walks memory in order",
        "A column steps n values at a time",
        "The transpose is A'(i,j) = A(j,i), which is the same block read the other way"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "What it costs you",
      "items": [
        "A multiplication costs m*n*p, and there is no trick here to make it less",
        "This is a library for small matrices, where the tricks cost more than they save",
        "Two allocators, thus a target with no heap can use every operation"
      ]
    }
  ]
